BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 712.0 Tm (Explanation: High prenatal pulmonary resistance diverts much right ventricular output through ductus arteriosus) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 698.9 Tm (into the aorta.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 682.8 Tm (Not A: Right-to-left atrial passage occurs at the foramen ovale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 669.4 Tm (Not C: Left ventricular output does not enter the portal vein.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 656.0 Tm (Not D: Umbilical venous diversion occurs at the ductus venosus.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 642.6 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q57 | 43-44; Chapter 27 ?2) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 619.4 Tm (55. At an otherwise unchanged capillary, how would increased interstitial protein concentration affect fluid) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 605.7 Tm (movement?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 589.0 Tm (Answer: D. It strengthens the outward oncotic force favouring filtration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 572.7 Tm (Explanation: More interstitial protein increases interstitial colloid osmotic pressure, tending to pull fluid) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 559.6 Tm (outward from the capillary and increase filtration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 543.5 Tm (Not A: Increased proteins outside the capillary attract rather than remove interstitial water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 530.1 Tm (Not B: Plasma protein concentration is held constant; the changed force is interstitial.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 516.7 Tm (Not C: A change in interstitial protein does not directly lower capillary pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 503.3 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q83 | 85-88) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 480.1 Tm (56. Electrical stimulation of the medullary pressor area increases arterial pressure. What is the principal) Tj ET
